@@ -0,0 +1,104 @@
+# Red-team attack on `parseCsvLine` — round 1
+
+Target: `parseCsvLine` in `src/csv.mjs` (working-tree version, the single-pass
+index scanner), against the contract in `README.md`. Node v25.2.1.
+
+Result: **no failing trace found**. `traces/` is empty (not created) because
+nothing reproduced. Verdict: pass.
+
+## Method
+
+Everything was run with `node --input-type=module` against the real module.
+Each probe was checked against the README by hand; the bulk runs were checked
+against an independent reference parser (a four-state character machine written
+from the README, not from the source: start / unquoted / quoted / after-quote,
+with one trailing `\n` or `\r\n` stripped first).
+
+### 1. Source review for boundary bugs
+
+Read the scanner for off-by-one and state errors around its `end` index:
+
+- `end` is only reduced when the last code unit is `\n` (then optionally the
+  `\r` before it). A lone trailing `\r` is therefore never stripped, and
+  `\n\r` strips nothing. Both match "any other unquoted `\r` or `\n` is a
+  `CsvError`".
+- In the quoted branch the escape look-ahead is guarded by `q + 1 < end`, so a
+  quote at `end - 1` is always a closing quote. Because the stripped tail can
+  only be `\n` / `\r\n`, `indexOf('"')` can never find a quote at or past `end`
+  (the `q >= end` guard is dead but harmless).
+- `j` after the inner loop is always `<= end`, so `i === end` is the only exit
+  and there is no way to read a comma from the stripped tail.
+- Trailing comma / empty text fall into the unquoted branch with `i === end`
+  and push `""`, giving `[""]` and `["a", ""]`.
+
+No defect found by reading.
+
+### 2. Exhaustive differential test
+
+All strings of length 0..8 over the alphabet `"` `,` `\n` `\r` `a`
+(488,281 inputs) compared with the reference parser: 0 mismatches. This covers
+every combination of terminator placement, quote escape run (`""`, `"""`,
+`""""`, ...), quote-after-content, quote-comma sequences, and terminator
+before/after a closing quote at every position the scanner can distinguish.
+
+### 3. Random differential fuzz
+
+- 300,000 strings of length 0..23 over a 16-symbol alphabet (the core five
+  plus space, tab, NUL, BOM, U+2028, U+0085, lone high and low surrogates,
+  `é`, and an astral pair): 0 mismatches. Also checked on every case: result is
+  a real `Array` with `Array.prototype`, no holes or extra properties, not
+  frozen, every element a primitive string; every throw is a `CsvError` that is
+  `instanceof Error` with `name === "CsvError"`; calling twice gives the same
+  result (determinism).
+- 500,000 strings of length 0..199 (quote-heavy alphabet, 30 % with a trailing
+  `\n` or `\r\n` appended) over five seeds: 0 mismatches.
+
+### 4. Targeted edge cases (all matched the README)
+
+Terminators: `""`→`[""]`; `\n`, `\r\n`→`[""]`; `\r`, `\n\r`, `\n\n`,
+`\r\n\r\n`, `\r\r\n`, `a\r`, `a\n\r`, `a\r\n\n`, `,\r` → CsvError;
+`a\n`, `a\r\n`, `,\n`, `,\r\n` strip one terminator.
+Quotes vs terminators: `"a"\n`, `"a"\r\n`→`["a"]`; `"a"\r`→CsvError (after
+closing quote); `"a\n`, `"a\r\n`→CsvError (unterminated); `"a\n"`→`["a\n"]`;
+`"a\r\n"`→`["a\r\n"]`; `"a\r"`→`["a\r"]`; `"a"\nb`, `"a"\r\nb`,
+`"a"\r\n\n`, `"a"\n\r\n`→CsvError.
+Escapes: `""`→`[""]`; `""""`→`['"']`; `""""""`→`['""']`; odd runs
+`"""`, `"""""`, `"""""""`, `""",`, `"a""`, `"a""\n`→CsvError;
+`"b""c"`→`['b"c']`; `"a,""b"",c"`→`['a,"b",c']`; `","`→`[","]`.
+Quotes after content / whitespace: `a"b`, `a "b"`, ` "b"`, `"b" `, `"b"c`,
+`a,"`, `a,"b`→CsvError; `"b", c`→`["b"," c"]`; `" a "`, tabs kept.
+Unicode: NUL, BOM, U+2028, U+2029, U+0085, VT, FF, lone surrogates (bare and
+inside quotes), astral pairs: all literal; `"a"` + lone surrogate → CsvError.
+Odd field names: `__proto__,constructor`, `toString`, `length` parse as plain
+strings; no prototype pollution observed.
+
+### 5. Non-string inputs
+
+`undefined`, no argument, `null`, number, NaN, boolean, BigInt, Symbol,
+`new String("a,b")`, arrays, objects with `toString` / `valueOf` /
+`Symbol.toPrimitive`, a `Proxy`, `Buffer`, function, `Date`, RegExp,
+`Object.create(null)`: every one throws `TypeError`. Extra arguments and
+`this === null` do not matter.
+
+### 6. Performance and exception type at scale
+
+Timed 24 pathological shapes at 100 KB, 1 MB and 10 MB: all quotes (even and
+odd count), all commas, one giant quoted field, one giant unquoted field, all
+`""` inside quotes, alternating `",` and `"",`, many quoted empty fields,
+`a,a,a,...`, unterminated giant fields (with and without commas), giant field
+followed by a bad character, giant quoted `\n` and `\r\n` runs, giant unquoted
+`\r` run, quote at the very end, astral pairs, lone surrogates, escaped-quote
+fields, trailing terminators on giant records, `"","` runs, `a"a"a...`.
+Worst case at 100 KB: 2.9 ms; at 10 MB: 271 ms. Only `CsvError` was ever
+thrown; no RangeError, stack overflow, or plain Error.
+
+### 7. Project suite
+
+`npm test`: 56/56 pass.
+
+## Not exercised
+
+- Tampering with `String.prototype` / `Array.prototype` builtins (outside the
+  contract: it promises behaviour for every string, not for a hostile realm).
+- Strings near V8's maximum length (~512 M code units); the contract only
+  bounds 100 KB and 10 MB already runs in a quarter of a second.
