+# Changes
+
+## Round 0
+
+round 0: no traces yet; initial hardening against the contract.
+
+### src/csv.mjs
+
+`parseCsvLine` was rewritten as a single-pass, index-based scanner. The old
+implementation toggled a `quoted` flag on every `"`, never threw `CsvError`,
+and re-sliced the remainder on every character (`rest.slice(1)`, O(n²)).
+
+Design decisions:
+
+- Exactly one trailing record terminator (`\n` or `\r\n`) is stripped
+  **before** parsing, by moving an `end` index. Consequences: `"a\n` becomes
+  `"a` and is an unterminated quote (CsvError); `"a\n"` ends in a quote, so
+  nothing is stripped and the `\n` is a literal character of the field;
+  `\n\n` strips one and hits an unquoted `\n` (CsvError); a bare trailing `\r`
+  is never stripped and is an unquoted `\r` (CsvError).
+- Quoted fields are scanned with `indexOf('"')` and chunk slices; `""` inside
+  quotes appends one `"`. After the closing quote only `,` or the end of
+  (stripped) text is accepted; anything else is a CsvError.
+- Unquoted fields run to the next `,`; a `"`, `\n` or `\r` anywhere in them is
+  a CsvError. Everything else (tabs, NUL, control chars, BOM, NEL, LS/PS,
+  surrogate pairs, lone surrogates) is literal, since the scan works on
+  UTF-16 code units and only ever compares against `"`, `,`, `\n`, `\r`.
+- No recursion, no regex, no repeated slicing: linear time and constant extra
+  stack, so no RangeError or stack overflow on any input size. Non-strings
+  (including `String` objects, `undefined`, symbols, BigInt, buffers,
+  objects with `toString`/`Symbol.toPrimitive`) throw `TypeError` before any
+  parsing.
+
+Measured: 100 KB pathological records (all quotes, all commas, one huge quoted
+field, many tiny fields, escaped-quote runs) parse in well under 10 ms; 10 MB
+versions in ~220 ms.
+
+### tests/csv.test.mjs
+
+Extended from 4 to 56 tests, grouped by contract line:
+
+- README examples
+- separators: empty text `[""]`, `a,` → `["a",""]`, leading/only commas
+- quoted fields: literal commas, `""` escapes (`""""` → `"`), `""` as an
+  empty field, `\n` / `\r\n` / bare `\r` literal inside quotes, quoted field
+  followed by a trailing terminator
+- after a closing quote: stray char/space/tab/NUL/extra quote → CsvError;
+  closing quote followed by unquoted `\r`, `\n\n`, `\n,b` → CsvError
+- unterminated quotes, including `"a\n`, `"a\r\n`, `"a""`, `"""`
+- `"` outside quotes: `a"b`, `a"b"`, `a "b"`, ` "a"`, `\t"a"` → CsvError
+- whitespace preserved (spaces, tabs, NBSP, ideographic space)
+- terminators: one trailing `\n` or `\r\n` removed (`\n` → `[""]`,
+  `"a"\r\n` → `["a"]`); bare trailing `\r`, doubled terminators, mixed
+  `\n\r\n` / `\r\r\n`, and any other unquoted `\r`/`\n` → CsvError
+- literal characters: tabs, NUL, C0/DEL controls, VT/FF, NEL, LS/PS, BOM,
+  curly quotes, fullwidth comma, combining marks, surrogate pairs, lone
+  surrogates
+- non-string input → TypeError (24 kinds, including `String` objects and
+  objects with `toString` / `Symbol.toPrimitive`), and TypeError is not a
+  CsvError
+- CsvError shape (instanceof Error, name, message) and result shape (fresh
+  array of primitive strings, no state between calls)
+- performance: 16 tests on 100 KB (and 1 MB) records, each asserting < 500 ms
+- differential testing against an independent char-by-char reference parser
+  written from the README: 20,000 random strings over a hostile alphabet,
+  plus an exhaustive sweep of all 19,531 strings up to length 6 over
+  `{", , \n \r a}`; and a 5,000-case fuzz over random UTF-16 code units
+  asserting only `string[]` or `CsvError` ever comes out.
+
+### Traces fixed
+
+None (round 0: no traces/ directory exists yet).
